## clinically-informed-support-with-families-at-the-centre | Why Families Choose MBP | Clinically Informed Support, With Families at the Centre | Why Families Choose MBP – Clinically Informed Support, With Families at the Centre
Michelle Barratt Psychology & Administration Services (MBP) provides a welcoming, neutral, and professionally managed entry point for families seeking psychological and allied health support.
- Clinically Informed Intake: Thoughtful intake processes help us understand your concerns and identify a suitable clinical pathway.
- Appropriate Practitioner Matching: We connect families with clinical psychologists, general psychologists, social workers, or counsellors whose experience aligns with child, adolescent, and family needs.
- Family-Focused Coordination: Our administration team assists parents and caregivers with appointment scheduling, intake requirements, and clear communication.
- Coordinated Care: Where appropriate and with your consent, practitioners can collaborate with GPs, paediatricians, schools, and other professionals involved in your child's care.
- Practical Referral Support: We assist with GP referral requirements, Mental Health Treatment Plans, and Medicare-related paperwork where applicable.
- Flexible Access: In-person appointments are available at our Brisbane clinics in Toowong and Manly West, alongside secure Online Therapy / Telehealth Australia-wide where clinically appropriate.
